A||N||5||87FieroGT||Questions for the Paint Pros??||||1||
Z||000000||87FieroGT||04-14-2000||12:26 AM||||I am getting ready to repaint my Fiero and I have a few questions. First of all I am going from a darker color to a lighter color and I need to know how far to sand the surfaces and if I need to use a primer or just the surfacer. I also need to know if it is better to use a base coat clear coat system on the Fiero body panels; or if a single stage urethane will work. What I am really worried about is scratches after the job is done. Thats about it I know there are a lot of other posts on painting, but these are specific questions and I don't have time to look through all of them. I need a direct response. Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||04-14-2000||12:37 AM||||To repaint from dark to light you need to reprime the whole car in a light color primer. We use the base coat clearcoat system here for the reason that after so many polishes you will go thru the paint whilt the clearcoat will not fade as easily. We also use PPG but you can use anything you brand you want. Just pick something that will last. PPG is sopposed to be a ten year paint.As far as sanding the best you could do is remove all the clear and make sure you clean the surface making sure you do not leave any grease or wax resedue.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-14-2000||12:33 PM||||To get rid of wax, you can use a chemical wax/dirt stripper made specificaly for this. That helps allot. Then after all the damaged areas are repaired sanded etc, go over every surface and scuff the paint. Try to get into crevases & seams at least a little.(blow out all the dust after.)<P>Scuffing helps make sure any fine surface bumps are gone. Also gives the new primer a really good bite. Nothing is more annoying than having new paint delaminate and peal off. All you need to do is make sure all the shine is gone. On big pannels a random orbital sander loaded with 600 or finer paper makes this real quick.<P>Depending on how much time you want to spend and the result you want. You can get really nice results by removing at least some panels for painting. Things like the door skins are good candidates. Then you'll be able to cover all the areas behind trim and mirrors, and around to the back side. Then you won't end up with corners that could flake and show the old color. You'll end up with a much more factory looking job when done.<P>Actually it might be faster to skin the doors than prep on the car. Like I said it all depends on your end goal and paint scheme. If I was changing the color I'd skin the door. The rest isn't to bad to work with but the doors have allot of ways they could show the old color later. I'd also take off any other trim moulding I could instead of trying to sand around it. With a color change if someone bumps the trim latter they could flake the paint and reveal the old color. It's real hard to sand next to the trim and be sure you've gotten it all. Worse there could be dirt under it that can come out while painting. Seems no matter how hard you try to clean there's always more under there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||87FieroGT||04-14-2000||07:06 PM||||Thanks for the info Ogre and fieroshop. I have a lot of work ahead of me. Ogre, I have not just taken off the door skins but all the other panels as well. The roof skin and the back GT clip are still on and I don't know if I am going to go through the trouble of taking them off or not. Anyway thanks again. I will post pictures when done.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||04-14-2000||07:38 PM||||I'd leave the roof for sure. you risk breaking it. The clip is pretty optional.||||reg||1
Z||000005||87FieroGT||04-15-2000||12:19 AM||||The roof is already broken in two places at the bottom. I can tell from the under body that this car has been in a wreck on the side and I think this is how it got broken. The only reason I was thinking of taking it off was to repair it easier and to get good coverage where the roof an the clip meet. Or do you think it might be better to leave the roof the way it is and not repair it. With all the other panels on you can't see the cracks. I didn't even know they were there until I took everything off. Thanks again Ogre.||||reg||1
